# Program Change in: GLO > MIDI > PC IN CH (OFF by default) and GLO > PC MAP (PC 0-127 -> a pattern, or "-").
# A PC on PC IN CH cues the pattern the map gives it for the next bar (at once when stopped), as PRESETS
# does; other channels, unmapped PCs, a song and the PERF test's own patterns change nothing. Here a drum
# machine sends its pattern PCs on channel 10 (112 = its bank 8, pattern 1) and its kit PC on channel 1.
wait 300
expect pcch 0
expect pcmapped 0
# OFF: a PC changes nothing, and the map does not see it
midi C9 70 00
wait 100
expect pattern 1
expect cue 0
expect pcsel 0
# PC IN CH 10 (GLO: the row after MIX MIDI CH)
tap GLO
turn SELECT 9
expect listsel 10
turn ALGO 10
expect pcch 10
shot pc01_glo_pc_in_ch.png
# a PC on 10 shows in the PC MAP (PC 112); unmapped, it changes nothing
midi C9 70 00
wait 100
expect pcsel 112
expect pattern 1
expect cue 0
# PATTERN (past the PC MAP header and the PC row): PC 112 -> P2
turn SELECT 2
expect listsel 13
turn ALGO 2
expect pcmap112 2
shot pc02_pc_map.png
# the next PC jumps the map to it, and a screen reader hears whose PATTERN it is now: PC 113 -> P3
listen
midi C9 71 00
wait 400
said PATTERN FOR PC 113 NONE
expect pcsel 113
spin ALGO 3
expect pcmap113 3
# PC 114 -> P20 (the second bank)
midi C9 72 00
wait 100
spin ALGO 20
expect pcmap114 20
expect pcmapped 3
# undo takes the map edit back, and says so (not "MOTION"); redo puts it back
wait 1500
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
wait 300
said UNDO PC MAP
expect pcmap114 0
press HOME
tap PLAY
release HOME
wait 300
expect pcmap114 20
tap HOME
tap HOME
expect view 0
# wrong channel: the kit PC on channel 1 (even with a mapped number)
midi C0 70 00
wait 100
expect pattern 1
expect cue 0
expect pcsel 114
# unmapped: PC 5 on channel 10
midi C9 05 00
wait 100
expect pcsel 5
expect pattern 1
expect cue 0
# mapped, stopped: at once, every part; a pattern in 17-32 takes HOME to that bank
midi C9 72 00
wait 100
expect pattern 20
expect ppat2 20
expect ppat4 20
expect pbank 1
midi C9 70 00
wait 100
expect pattern 2
expect pbank 0
expect cue 0
# mapped, playing: cued (HOME's box blinks), every part lands when the 909's bar ends (125 BPM: 1.92 s)
tap PLAY
wait 300
midi C9 71 00
wait 100
expect cue 3
expect pattern 2
shot pc03_home_cue.png
wait 1400
expect pattern 2
expect ppat3 2
wait 250
expect pattern 3
expect ppat3 3
expect ppat4 3
expect cue 0
tap PLAY
wait 100
# it ends a chain: P1-P4 chained, PC 113 -> P3 in the first bar; the chain alone would play P2, then P4
expect view 0
key w0 down
key w3 down
wait 50
key w3 up
key w0 up
wait 100
expect pattern 1
tap PLAY
wait 300
midi C9 71 00
wait 1750
expect pattern 3
wait 1920
expect pattern 3
tap PLAY
wait 100
# the PERF test plays three patterns of its own: a PC during it changes nothing, and the test ends
tap GLO
turn SELECT 21
tap SEL
expect view 7
tap SEL
turn SELECT 1
tap SEL
wait 300
expect perftest 0
expect patptr 0
midi C9 72 00
wait 100
expect cue 0
wait 5600
midi C9 72 00
wait 5000
midi C9 71 00
wait 100
expect cue 0
wait 6000
expect perftest 3
expect patptr 1
expect pattern 3
tap HOME
# kept: SAVE, then power on again
tap SAVE
wait 1500
reboot
wait 300
expect pcch 10
expect pcmap112 2
expect pcmap113 3
expect pcmap114 20
expect pcmapped 3
midi C9 70 00
wait 100
expect pattern 2
# the SONG screen with a song: the song decides, so a PC is ignored, stopped or playing
tap HOME
tap HOME
expect view 6
tapkey w0
tapkey w0
expect songlen 2
midi C9 71 00
wait 100
expect pattern 2
expect cue 0
turn K1 -5
tap PLAY
expect songon 1
wait 300
midi C9 71 00
wait 100
expect cue 0
tap PLAY
wait 100
# recording the song, a PC is written into it like PRESETS: bar 2 gets P3
tap REC
turn K1 -5
tap PLAY
wait 300
midi C9 71 00
wait 1800
expect pattern 3
tap PLAY
tap REC
wait 100
expect songbar2.0 3
